kdc5072@ultb.isc.rit.edu (K.D. Colagio) writes:

>M.E. Donnaruma writes:
>->      Well, I'm wondering how to get into Wizard mode, just to see it,
>-> and well, I saw a post awhile back that said to type:
>-> 	nethack -uwizard-D   
>-> 
>-> 	NOPE! That's just plain old Discovery mode (or was it nothing?)
>-> anyways, what is the REAL command to get into wiz mode?
>-> 
>This will only work (on a unix type machine) if your user name is
>wizard...at least that is what it seems like.

>I went through at compilation and set it (in config.h) to "games".  I
>then made a user (on my own unix machine) named games.  I use that
>"user" when I want to be in wizard mode...no problems...

>If you are on a DOS machine, I have no idea...(same with macs, amigas,
>ataris, etc...)

No, it works fine on a DOS machine.

Use 

nethack -uwizard   -D

You need to put the space there for it to work on a DOS
machine.
